WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.123 --> 00:00:05.330
- Right now, we're hearing
the sun just start

00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:09.497
to activate the UV sensors
on the outdoor sensor unit.

00:00:12.851 --> 00:00:15.518
It started about 10 minutes ago.

00:00:17.664 --> 00:00:20.502
That puttering sound is
the sound of that sensor

00:00:20.502 --> 00:00:24.669
just starting to get enough
light to sonically activate it,

00:00:26.772 --> 00:00:29.775
and the puttering will
eventually turn into a note,

00:00:29.775 --> 00:00:32.397
and that note will semitone by semitone,

00:00:32.397 --> 00:00:36.154
increase in pitch until
it becomes inaudible,

00:00:36.154 --> 00:00:38.847
and then it'll be inaudible all day long,

00:00:38.847 --> 00:00:43.341
until the UV drops to a
point when you can hear it.

00:00:43.341 --> 00:00:45.630
Again, usually at sunset,
but if it's a cloudy

00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:49.130
or rainy day, it'll activate all day long.

00:00:50.778 --> 00:00:54.451
We've just completed helicopter mode.

00:00:54.451 --> 00:00:58.235
First it sounds like
drums, then it sounds like

00:00:58.235 --> 00:01:01.818
a helicopter, now it
sounds like a monster.

00:01:05.787 --> 00:01:07.620
Soon it will be music.

00:01:10.685 --> 00:01:13.602
(pulsating sounds)

00:01:30.617 --> 00:01:32.200
This is the mixers.

00:01:44.599 --> 00:01:45.432
Yeah.

00:01:50.007 --> 00:01:52.411
And this is just the global
delay on that whole thing

00:01:52.411 --> 00:01:55.828
to give it, to give the sound some depth.

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:09.497
(humming)

00:02:09.497 --> 00:02:12.470
Nothing really is happening.

00:02:12.470 --> 00:02:15.915
It's not windy or raining,
or anything very exciting,

00:02:15.915 --> 00:02:17.657
weather-wise, but this music is something

00:02:17.657 --> 00:02:20.907
that is to be almost breathed like air,

00:02:23.638 --> 00:02:25.638
or bathed in like water.

00:02:28.641 --> 00:02:31.368
But now you can hear the
sun tone is now in key

00:02:31.368 --> 00:02:32.701
with this chord.

00:02:33.551 --> 00:02:36.435
(humming)

00:02:36.435 --> 00:02:37.268
Hear it.

00:02:38.888 --> 00:02:42.840
It's on E, and it'll fall out of phase.

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:44.840
I'll turn the delay off.

00:02:45.976 --> 00:02:47.809
This is the cool shit.

00:03:00.888 --> 00:03:03.971
(music notes rising)

